 "notes": "Lower boundary (energy-loss floor) of the solid black SN1987A excluded region in Figure 3, extracted from the vector paths of SN.pdf in the arXiv e-print with axes calibrated on tick labels (m in MeV converted to eV, epsilon = kinetic mixing). This is the paper's new supernova cooling bound on dark photons including plasma mixing effects (Raffelt criterion eps_new < 1e19 erg/g/s for their representative SN model of ref [21]); the paper stresses these are order-of-magnitude estimates, not a statistical CL, so confidence_level=0.95 is nominal. The excluded region also has an upper boundary (ceiling from trapping/absorption and e+e- decays, region above eps~1e-7..1e-5 not excluded), which meets the floor at m~4e8 eV where the region closes; only the floor is reported here. The floor dips to eps~5.8e-11 at m~17 MeV due to resonant transverse emission near the SN core plasma frequency (~20 MeV). No dark-matter density assumed (cooling bound). Other bounds in the paper (B-L vector solar bound Fig 4, scalar-electron/nucleon Fig 5, Higgs-portal Fig 6) were not chosen; the SN dark photon constraint is the paper's most prominent new exclusion.",
